{# What a folder action that worked answers with (#221): New folder, rename,
   delete.

   The toast is the app's own, the one sent mail and label changes use, so the
   result is said where every other result is said. Both copies of the sidebar
   are re-rendered whole, as LabelController's refreshSidebar does: a folder
   lives in two places there — under its account, and as a label under LABELS —
   and a list only one of them refreshed would contradict the other until the
   next page load. A stream whose target is absent (Settings has no sidebar
   drawer open, say) is a no-op.

   New folder and rename answer with this alone, as a turbo-stream, and the
   modal closes on them like on any form. Delete is pressed inside the folder
   list, which stays open: it answers with the list, and this rides inside it
   (_folders_modal.html.twig, `done`).

   Variables:
     toast    string  already translated #}
{% include '_partials/_toast.stream.html.twig' with { message: toast, type: 'success' } only %}

<turbo-stream action="replace" target="sidebar">
    <template>
        {% include '_partials/_sidebar.html.twig' only %}
    </template>
</turbo-stream>
<turbo-stream action="replace" target="sidebar-drawer-inner">
    <template>
        {% include '_partials/_sidebar.html.twig' with { _drawerMode: true } only %}
    </template>
</turbo-stream>
